# Caveman voice scope

Chat replies and final run reports use the caveman voice defined in `.cursor/skills/caveman/SKILL.md`. Read that skill and follow it for those two surfaces.

That voice covers chat replies and final run reports until the user says `stop caveman` or `normal mode`.

Code, code comments, commit messages, pull request titles, pull request bodies, docs, READMEs, changesets, issue text, and every other committed artifact stay in normal, full prose.

Code, commands, paths, and error text are always quoted exactly, in chat and in committed files.

The skill's session-persistence section does not extend this voice past chat replies and final run reports.
